  Though a simple enough concept―incapacitate a patrol, steal their uniforms, then stride into the enemy base unhindered―it is not nearly as easy as spy thrillers make it seem.

  Will we find two soldiers whose uniforms fit? Can we disable them before they raise the alarm? Can we convince the men at the checkpoint that we're friendly? There are too many ways for it to go wrong.

